T*
(actually decides careers: the decision letter that says Major Revision. For many) Tj
T*
(early-career academics in India and other emerging research systems, this letter arrives as) Tj
T*
(a shock. It is long. It is contradictory. It is sometimes rude. And it is, more often than) Tj
T*
(not, the last gate between you and a Scopus- or WoS-indexed publication that your) Tj
T*
(institution will count.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Here is the truth most workshops skip: a major revision is not a polite rejection. It is a) Tj
T*
(conditional invitation. Editors have already spent scarce reviewer time on you. They would) Tj
T*
(rather accept a repaired paper than start the search again. Your job is not to win an) Tj
T*
(argument. Your job is to make acceptance the path of least resistance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This playbook gives you a 21-day operating system: how to read the letter without panic, how) Tj
T*
(to classify every comment, how to write a rebuttal that reviewers can scan in eight minutes,) Tj
T*
(and how to revise the manuscript so the editor can defend you in the next round.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. FIRST, DECODE THE DECISION - NOT THE TONE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The first 24 hours after a decision letter are emotionally expensive and intellectually) Tj
T*
(cheap. Do not open a blank Word file. Do not draft a defensive email to the editor. Print) Tj
T*
(the letter, or paste it into a two-column table, and classify every numbered and unnumbered) Tj
T*
(point.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use four buckets only:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Must-fix. The editor repeated it, or two reviewers independently raised it. These decide) Tj
T*
(the paper.) Tj
T*
(- Should-fix. One reviewer, but the request is reasonable and cheap: clarity, extra) Tj
T*
(robustness check, missing citation.) Tj
T*
(- Negotiate. The request would change the research question, demand unavailable data, or) Tj
T*
(contradict another reviewer.) Tj
T*
(- Ignore-with-courtesy. Taste comments such as 'I would have written a different paper'.) Tj
T*
(Acknowledge, explain why you did not rebuild the house, move on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If the editor's cover note highlights two or three issues, those two or three issues are the) Tj
T*
(exam. Reviewer 3's eleventh suggestion is not. Early-career authors often treat every) Tj
T*
(sentence as equal. Editors do not.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Field rule: If Reviewer 1 and Reviewer 2 disagree, do not pick a winner in private. Write) Tj
T*
(both interpretations in the response letter, state the criterion you used - theory,) Tj
T*
(identification, sample constraints, journal aim and scope - and show the manuscript change) Tj
T*
(that follows from that criterion. Editors reward explicit reasoning more than loyalty to the) Tj
T*
(louder reviewer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. BUILD A COMMENT LEDGER BEFORE YOU REWRITE A SINGLE PARAGRAPH) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A revision fails when the manuscript and the response letter drift apart. Prevent that with) Tj
T*
(a living spreadsheet - the Comment Ledger. One row per comment. Six columns:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- ID: R1.3, R2.1, Ed.2. Lets the editor jump, not hunt.) Tj
T*
(- Verbatim ask: copy the reviewer's sentence, lightly trimmed. Stops you from answering a) Tj
